1169891357,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":87.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.00698,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"H&R Block, Inc., through its subsidiaries, provides assisted and do-it-yourself (DIY) tax preparation solutions in the United States, Canada, and Australia. The company offers tax preparation services, such as assisted income tax return preparation and related services through a system of retail offices operated directly or through its franchisees in person or virtually; refund transfers for clients to receive tax refunds; Peace of Mind, an extended service plan; and H&R Block Emerald Prepaid Mastercard and Spruce debit cards. It also provides H&R Block Emerald Advance, a term loan; Tax Identity Shield, a program for protection of tax identity and access to services to help restore tax identity; refund advance loans; H&R Block's Instant Refund, an advance refund; and small business financial solutions, such as payment processing, payroll and bookkeeping services. H&R Block, Inc. was incorporated in 1955 and is headquartered in Kansas City, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Curtis A. Campbell | CEO, President & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $858K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $164K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["H&R Block, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $6.1B market cap on $3.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 118% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 111-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $756M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.14\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 11.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (18.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"News sentiment sharply negative (-0.39) across 12 recent articles \u2014 the narrative has turned","sev":"red","cat":"news"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 30% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 16% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 69% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 27% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"H&R Block (HRB) reports Q3: everything you need to know ahead of earnings","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/h-r-block-hrb-reports-152536434.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794324336.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.7,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"H&R Block (HRB) Reaffirmed Guidance, Is It Still Only Slightly Undervalued?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nyse-hrb/hr-block/news/hr-block-hrb-reaffirmed-guidance-is-it-still-only-slightly-u","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794320459.5,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"H&R Block reaffirms FY2027 outlook of $4.11B-$4.16B revenue while expanding consultative model test to ~650 offices (NYSE:HRB)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4669493-h-and-r-block-reaffirms-fy2027-outlook-of-4_11b-4_16b-revenue-while-expanding-consultative","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794288818.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.307,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"HRB Q3 CY2026 deep dive: digital service expansion and cost pressures shape outlook","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nyse/hrb/news/earnings-call/hrb-q3-cy2026-deep-dive-digital-service-expansion-and-cost-pressures-shape-outlook","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794288800.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.637,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"H&R Block (HRB) Reports Q1 Loss, Beats Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3026827/h-r-block-hrb-reports-q1-loss-beats-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3026827","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794263705.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.637,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"AQR Capital Management Discloses 6.10% Stake in H&R Block in Amended SEC Filing","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/aqr-capital-management-discloses-610-stake-in-hr-block-in-amended-sec-filing","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794584007.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.44,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"H&R Block Q1 Earnings Call Highlights","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/hr-block-q1-earnings-call-highlights.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794496649.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.026,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"H&R Block Q1 Earnings Meet Estimates, Revenues Increase 10% Y/Y","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3027445/h-r-block-q1-earnings-meet-estimates-revenues-increase-10-y-y?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cearnings_article-3027445","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794336840.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.153,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"H&R Block Emerald Advance Loan offers up to $1,750 now through Dec. 30","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://fina